  "title": "NSE IPO prices likely to adjust with OFS reduction",
  "summary": "The NSE IPO may shrink to Rs 25,000-27,000 crore as OFS is likely to be cut, with prices potentially dropping below the previous estimate of Rs 30,000 crore. This reduction could affect the overall size and attractiveness of the offering, with the NSE aiming to attract retail investors.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The OFS may be reduced to 5.2-5.5 per cent from the original 6 per cent as some shareholders withdraw from the sale.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The reduced OFS could bring down the overall issue size to Rs 25,000-27,000 crore, compared with the earlier estimate of Rs 30,000 crore.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The NSE is also looking to make the issue more attractive for retail investors, with pricing being structured to provide greater participation and benefit to small investors in the OFS",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
